    "chapter_name": "Center of Mass Momentum and Collision",
    "year": "2022",
    "shift": "shift_1"
  },
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A pendulum of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> consists of a wooden bob of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>. A bullet of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>75</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> is fired towards the stationary bob with a speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math>. The bullet emerges out of the bob with a speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>v</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math> and the bob just completes the vertical circle. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math> is _____&nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>(if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>).</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "10",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>For the bob to completer the vertical circle, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn><mi>g</mi><mi>l</mi></msqrt></math>.</p><p>From the conservation of momentum,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mfrac><mi>v</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>75</mn><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><msqrt><mn>5</mn><mi>g</mi><mi>l</mi></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>75</mn><mfenced><mfrac><mi>v</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>75</mn><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>v</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><msqrt><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>75</mn><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>v</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>10</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>500</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>150</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>500</mn><mn>50</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p>"
  }
}